{
  "name": "Review and approve supplier applications with OpenAI, Google Sheets and Gmail",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "sn-main",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -900,
        -400
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 1,
        "width": 480,
        "height": 900,
        "content": "## Review and approve new suppliers with AI, Google Sheets, Discord and Gmail\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow watches a Google Sheet where your team logs new supplier applications. When a row is added, it validates the required fields, then an AI agent reviews the application: it checks that the data is complete, assigns a risk level and a category, and recommends whether to approve the supplier, request more information, or reject the application. Every review is appended to a Supplier Log sheet, and the outcome is routed: approved suppliers get an approval email and the team is notified on Discord, while applications that need more information or look risky trigger a Discord alert to procurement and an email asking the requester for the missing details. A monthly scheduled run summarizes all supplier reviews from the sheet and sends the report by email and to Discord.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Create a Google Sheet with a SupplierApplications sheet using the headers: application_id, company_name, contact_name, contact_email, category, annual_value, documents_ok, status, received_at.\n- Connect Google Sheets credentials and set the spreadsheet and sheet name in the trigger and log nodes.\n- Connect Gmail credentials for the approval and review emails.\n- Connect Discord credentials and choose the channel where the team should be alerted.\n- Connect your OpenAI credential to the AI agent so it can evaluate applications.\n\n### Customization\n\n- Change the AI prompt in the review agent to match your approval policy.\n- Adjust the monthly summary cron expression to run on your preferred schedule.\n- Add extra fields to the sheet and map them in the normalize step.\n- Switch the review email recipients by editing the Gmail node addresses."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "sn-intake",
      "name": "Sticky Note: Intake",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -400,
        -520
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 420,
        "height": 200,
        "content": "## Intake\n\nA new row in the SupplierApplications sheet starts the flow. Required fields are validated and invalid applications are flagged on Discord."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "sn-ai",
      "name": "Sticky Note: AI review",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        240,
        -520
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 420,
        "height": 200,
        "content": "## AI review\n\nAn AI agent evaluates the supplier application, extracts a category and risk level, and recommends approve, request more info, or reject."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "sn-routing",
      "name": "Sticky Note: Decision routing",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        920,
        -520
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 480,
        "height": 200,
        "content": "## Decision routing\n\nReviews are logged to the Supplier Log sheet. Suppliers that need more info or look risky alert procurement on Discord and email the requester; the rest get an approval email and a Discord confirmation."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
